<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in the `va_log` function, which is called by the `ERROR` macro. The `va_log` function attempts to call `parser->callb.log_func`, which is a null pointer.

The fuzz driver creates a `usbredirparser` object and initializes some of its function pointers, but it fails to initialize `log_func`. The `usbredirparser_init` function does not set a default logger.

To fix this, the fuzz driver should be modified to provide a `log_func` during the initialization of the `usbredirparser` object. A dummy logging function that does nothing would be sufficient to prevent the crash.

```c
static void dummy_log(void *priv, int level, const char *str) {
// A dummy log function that does nothing.
}

...

extern "C" int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *data, size_t size) {
...
parser->log_func = dummy_log;
...
}
```
</crash-analysis>

